  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656040",
      "title": "Creating an \"Ingredient\" Model",
      "lectureOrder": 381,
      "videoOrder": 351,
      "sourceHash": "a15aad3ea97c7d02445c93e54affb981614f4a4f77fccd093f9e451cef570830",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 5.67,
          "en": "-: We're going to use ingredients a lot in our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.67,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "so having a model for it makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 10.517,
          "en": "Now, where do we store this ingredient model?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.517,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "We store the recipe model in the recipes folder because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 16.021,
          "en": "it belongs there feature-wise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.021,
          "end": 20.623,
          "en": "But where does the ingredient model belong to?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.623,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "Well, I believe it belongs in a new folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 26.37,
          "en": "The shared folder, which I'm going to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.37,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "in the app folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 31.38,
          "en": "Shared is a fitting name for this folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 35.73,
          "en": "because it will contain features or elements of our app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "which are shared across different features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 41.28,
          "en": "Like the ingredient, which we're going to use both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.28,
          "end": 44.088,
          "en": "in the shopping list and the recipe section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.088,
          "end": 45.963,
          "en": "So here I'll trade a new file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.963,
          "end": 49.18,
          "en": "and this file will be named ingredient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "dot model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 52.89,
          "en": "dot ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 56.826,
          "en": "In there I will export a class named ingredient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.826,
          "end": 57.707,
          "en": "and here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.707,
          "end": 61.83,
          "en": "we will basically define how an ingredient should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.83,
          "end": 63.28,
          "en": "Now, how should it look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.29,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "It should have a name, so publicly available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "which is a string and an amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "So how many items of that type should we have?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 77.163,
          "en": "So maybe amount here, which would be of type number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.21000000000001,
          "end": 81.27,
          "en": "Now in the constructor, we of course want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.27,
          "end": 85.026,
          "en": "be able to receive that as arguments name and amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.026,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "and then assign it here as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 91.759,
          "en": "So this name equals name and this amount equals amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.759,
          "end": 94.77000000000001,
          "en": "Now that is such a typical setup that we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.77000000000001,
          "end": 97.86,
          "en": "receive the arguments we want to assign in the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.86,
          "end": 99.493,
          "en": "and that instantly assign them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.493,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "That type script offers a shortcut.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "We can get rid of the declaration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "of our properties up here and get rid of the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 114.096,
          "en": "in the body of this constructor and simply add an accessor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.096,
          "end": 116.843,
          "en": "in front of the property name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.843,
          "end": 120.193,
          "en": "so public in front of both arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.193,
          "end": 121.5,
          "en": "What that will do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.5,
          "end": 124.435,
          "en": "is behind the scenes it will create the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.435,
          "end": 126.54,
          "en": "effect we had before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.54,
          "end": 129.534,
          "en": "So it will automatically give us properties with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.534,
          "end": 133.08,
          "en": "the names we specify here as argument names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 135.15,
          "en": "So name and amount in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.15,
          "end": 138.6,
          "en": "And it'll automatically assign the values we receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.6,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "in this constructor to these newly created properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 144.78300000000002,
          "en": "So nice and convenient shortcut.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.62,
          "end": 148.86,
          "en": "With that, we defined how an ingredient should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.86,
          "end": 151.26,
          "en": "Now we can use it in this shopping list component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.26,
          "end": 153.69299999999998,
          "en": "Let's do this in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
